### ==============================================================
### CatalogService — OData V4 & V2 test scenarios (REST Client)
### ==============================================================
### Start the server first:  npx cds watch
### V4 base: http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog
### V2 base: http://localhost:4004/odata/v2/catalog  (via @cap-js-community/odata-v2-adapter)
###
### AUTH NOTE (verified against a live server):
### CatalogService requires role 'authenticated-user' on the service,
### and @restrict roles 'Admin' / 'Traveller' (capitalised) on
### Travellers & TravelledLocations. Role checks are case-sensitive,
### and the project ships no custom mock users yet — the CAP default
### mocked users (alice/bob/carol/dave/erin/fred/me/yves) only carry
### lowercase 'admin' / 'cds.ExtensionDeveloper' roles, so every
### @adminUser / @traveller1User / @traveller2User request below will
### 403 until you add matching mock users. Add a project-root
### `.cdsrc.json` (untracked, dev-only; not in .gitignore yet — see
### chat) with:
###
### {
###   "requires": { "auth": { "kind": "mocked", "users": {
###     "admin":         { "roles": ["Admin"] },
###     "rohan.sharma":  { "roles": ["Traveller"] },
###     "emily.johnson": { "roles": ["Traveller"] }
###   } } }
### }
###
### rohan.sharma / emily.johnson match the `userID` column in
### db/data/burhan.claude-Travellers.csv, so $user-based row filtering
### can be exercised for real.

@host = http://localhost:4004
@v4 = {{host}}/odata/v4/catalog
@v2 = {{host}}/odata/v2/catalog

@adminUser = admin
@adminPass = pass
@traveller1User = rohan.sharma
@traveller1Pass = pass
@traveller2User = emily.johnson
@traveller2Pass = pass

# Traveller 1 = rohan.sharma's own row; Traveller 2 = emily.johnson's own row
@travellerID = 10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@traveller2ID = 10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002
@destinationID = 30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@locationID = 40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001


### ==============================================================
### A. Destinations — open to any authenticated user; Create + Read
###    only, Update/Delete rejected with 405 (srv/catalog-service.ts)
### ==============================================================

### A1. [V4] List all destinations
GET {{v4}}/Destinations
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### A2. [V4] Read one destination
GET {{v4}}/Destinations({{destinationID}})
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### A3. [V4] Create a destination (any authenticated user)
# @name createDestinationV4
POST {{v4}}/Destinations
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Lisbon Coastal Trip",
  "country": "Portugal",
  "city": "Lisbon",
  "region": "Lisbon District",
  "description": "Coastal towns, trams and pastel de nata tasting."
}

### A4. [V4] Update destination — expect 405 (immutable per spec 3.4)
PATCH {{v4}}/Destinations({{destinationID}})
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "region": "Changed Region" }

### A5. [V4] Delete destination — expect 405 (immutable per spec 3.4)
DELETE {{v4}}/Destinations({{destinationID}})
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### A6. [V2] List all destinations
GET {{v2}}/Destinations
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### A7. [V2] Create a destination
POST {{v2}}/Destinations
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Reykjavik Northern Lights",
  "country": "Iceland",
  "city": "Reykjavik",
  "region": "Capital Region",
  "description": "Aurora watching and the Golden Circle route."
}

### A8. [V2] Update destination via MERGE — expect 405
MERGE {{v2}}/Destinations({{destinationID}})
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "region": "Changed Region" }

### A9. [V2] Delete destination — expect 405
DELETE {{v2}}/Destinations({{destinationID}})
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### A10. [V4] Unauthenticated request — expect 401
GET {{v4}}/Destinations


### ==============================================================
### B. Value-help code lists — @readonly: TravellerTypes,
###    TravellerStatus, AddressTypes
### ==============================================================

### B1. [V4] List traveller types
GET {{v4}}/TravellerTypes
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### B2. [V4] List traveller status value help
GET {{v4}}/TravellerStatus
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### B3. [V4] List address types value help
GET {{v4}}/AddressTypes
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### B4. [V4] Attempt to create a traveller type — expect 405 (@readonly)
POST {{v4}}/TravellerTypes
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "VIP", "name": "VIP", "descr": "VIP traveller" }

### B5. [V2] List traveller types
GET {{v2}}/TravellerTypes
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### B6. [V2] Attempt to update a traveller type — expect 405 (@readonly)
MERGE {{v2}}/TravellerTypes('FF')
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Changed" }


### ==============================================================
### C. Travellers — Create/Read/Update (no Delete per spec 3.1);
###    computed fullName, etag concurrency, row-level security
### ==============================================================

### C1. [V4] Admin reads all travellers
GET {{v4}}/Travellers
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### C2. [V4] Traveller reads own row — 200
GET {{v4}}/Travellers({{travellerID}})
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### C3. [V4] Traveller reads someone else's row — expect 404 (row filtered out)
GET {{v4}}/Travellers({{traveller2ID}})
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### C4. [V4] Traveller lists all travellers — only own row comes back
GET {{v4}}/Travellers
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### C5. [V4] Create traveller — missing firstName — expect 400
POST {{v4}}/Travellers
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "jane.doe@travelapp.com",
  "type_code": "STD",
  "status_code": "A",
  "userID": "jane.doe"
}

### C6. [V4] Create traveller — attempt to set computed fullName — expect 400
POST {{v4}}/Travellers
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "fullName": "Jane Doe",
  "email": "jane.doe@travelapp.com",
  "type_code": "STD",
  "status_code": "A",
  "userID": "jane.doe"
}

### C7. [V4] Create traveller — duplicate email — expect 409
POST {{v4}}/Travellers
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Duplicate",
  "lastName": "Rohan",
  "email": "rohan.sharma@travelapp.com",
  "type_code": "STD",
  "status_code": "A",
  "userID": "duplicate.rohan"
}

### C8. [V4] Create traveller — happy path — expect 201, fullName enriched on read-back
# @name createTravellerV4
POST {{v4}}/Travellers
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "jane.doe@travelapp.com",
  "phone": "+1-555-0100",
  "addressType_code": "H",
  "type_code": "STD",
  "status_code": "A",
  "userID": "jane.doe"
}

### C9. [V4] Filter on computed fullName — expect 400 (blocked by before-READ handler)
GET {{v4}}/Travellers?$filter=fullName eq 'Rohan Sharma'
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### C10. [V4] Sort by computed fullName — expect 400
GET {{v4}}/Travellers?$orderby=fullName
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### C11. [V4] Get own row to capture ETag for optimistic concurrency
# @name getTravellerV4
GET {{v4}}/Travellers({{travellerID}})
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### C12. [V4] Update without If-Match header — expect 428
PATCH {{v4}}/Travellers({{travellerID}})
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "+91-90000-00000" }

### C13. [V4] Update own row with captured ETag — expect 200
PATCH {{v4}}/Travellers({{travellerID}})
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}
If-Match: {{getTravellerV4.response.headers.ETag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "+91-90000-00000" }

### C14. [V4] Traveller tries to update someone else's row — expect 404 (not visible)
GET {{v4}}/Travellers({{traveller2ID}})
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### C15. [V4] Traveller attempts DELETE — expect 403 (not granted to Traveller role)
DELETE {{v4}}/Travellers({{travellerID}})
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### C16. [V4] Admin attempts DELETE — note: @restrict grants Admin '*' so this is
###      NOT blocked by role, but etag concurrency still applies (expect 428
###      without If-Match). Spec 3.1 says delete should never be permitted —
###      this is a gap in the current @restrict config worth flagging.
DELETE {{v4}}/Travellers({{traveller2ID}})
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### C17. [V2] Admin reads all travellers
GET {{v2}}/Travellers
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### C18. [V2] Traveller reads own row
GET {{v2}}/Travellers(guid'{{travellerID}}')
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### C19. [V2] Create traveller — happy path
POST {{v2}}/Travellers
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Smith",
  "email": "john.smith.v2@travelapp.com",
  "phone": "+1-555-0199",
  "addressType_code": "O",
  "type_code": "STD",
  "status_code": "A",
  "userID": "john.smith.v2"
}

### C20. [V2] Get own row to capture ETag (V2 date/time literals differ from V4)
# @name getTravellerV2
GET {{v2}}/Travellers(guid'{{travellerID}}')
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### C21. [V2] Update via MERGE without If-Match — expect 428
MERGE {{v2}}/Travellers(guid'{{travellerID}}')
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "+91-90000-11111" }

### C22. [V2] Update via MERGE with captured ETag — expect 200/204
MERGE {{v2}}/Travellers(guid'{{travellerID}}')
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}
If-Match: {{getTravellerV2.response.headers.ETag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "+91-90000-11111" }

### C23. [V2] Duplicate email — expect 409
POST {{v2}}/Travellers
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Duplicate",
  "lastName": "Emily",
  "email": "emily.johnson@travelapp.com",
  "type_code": "STD",
  "status_code": "A",
  "userID": "duplicate.emily"
}


### ==============================================================
### D. TravelledLocations — Create/Read/Delete (no Update);
###    date-range validation, overlap check, row-level security
### ==============================================================

### D1. [V4] Admin reads all travelled locations, expanding traveller & destination
GET {{v4}}/TravelledLocations?$expand=traveller,destination
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### D2. [V4] Traveller reads own travelled locations only
GET {{v4}}/TravelledLocations?$filter=traveller_ID eq {{travellerID}}
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### D3. [V4] Create — travelFrom after travelTo — expect 400
POST {{v4}}/TravelledLocations
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "traveller_ID": "{{travellerID}}",
  "destination_ID": "{{destinationID}}",
  "travelFrom": "2027-01-20",
  "travelTo": "2027-01-10",
  "notes": "Invalid date range"
}

### D4. [V4] Create — overlaps an existing trip for the same traveller — expect 409
###      (rohan.sharma already has a trip 2026-10-05..2026-10-12, see
###      db/data/burhan.claude-TravelledLocations.csv)
POST {{v4}}/TravelledLocations
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "traveller_ID": "{{travellerID}}",
  "destination_ID": "{{destinationID}}",
  "travelFrom": "2026-10-08",
  "travelTo": "2026-10-15",
  "notes": "Overlaps existing Paris trip"
}

### D5. [V4] Create — happy path, non-overlapping dates — expect 201
# @name createLocationV4
POST {{v4}}/TravelledLocations
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "traveller_ID": "{{travellerID}}",
  "destination_ID": "{{destinationID}}",
  "travelFrom": "2028-01-05",
  "travelTo": "2028-01-12",
  "notes": "Follow-up trip, no overlap"
}

### D6. [V4] Delete a travelled location — expect 204
DELETE {{v4}}/TravelledLocations({{locationID}})
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### D7. [V4] Update a travelled location — expect 405 (not supported, no handler; generic PATCH allowed unless blocked)
PATCH {{v4}}/TravelledLocations({{locationID}})
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "notes": "Trying to edit an immutable travel log entry" }

### D8. [V2] List with $expand
GET {{v2}}/TravelledLocations?$expand=traveller,destination
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}

### D9. [V2] Create — overlap check — expect 409
POST {{v2}}/TravelledLocations
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "traveller_ID": "{{travellerID}}",
  "destination_ID": "{{destinationID}}",
  "travelFrom": "2026-10-06",
  "travelTo": "2026-10-09",
  "notes": "Overlaps existing Paris trip (V2)"
}

### D10. [V2] Delete a travelled location
POST {{v2}}/TravelledLocations
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "traveller_ID": "{{travellerID}}",
  "destination_ID": "{{destinationID}}",
  "travelFrom": "2029-02-01",
  "travelTo": "2029-02-07",
  "notes": "Created via V2 for delete test"
}


### ==============================================================
### E. Query options — $filter / $orderby / $expand / $select /
###    $top / $skip / $count (V4) vs $inlinecount (V2)
### ==============================================================

### E1. [V4] $select + $top + $skip
GET {{v4}}/Destinations?$select=name,city,country&$top=3&$skip=2
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### E2. [V4] $filter with contains()
GET {{v4}}/Destinations?$filter=contains(country,'France')
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### E3. [V4] $expand nested (Travellers -> locations -> destination)
GET {{v4}}/Travellers({{travellerID}})?$expand=locations($expand=destination)
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### E4. [V4] $count=true inline
GET {{v4}}/Destinations?$count=true
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### E5. [V4] /$count resource
GET {{v4}}/Destinations/$count
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### E6. [V2] $select + $top + $skip
GET {{v2}}/Destinations?$select=name,city,country&$top=3&$skip=2
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### E7. [V2] $filter with substringof (classic V2 filter function)
GET {{v2}}/Destinations?$filter=substringof('France',country)
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### E8. [V2] $inlinecount=allpages
GET {{v2}}/Destinations?$inlinecount=allpages
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}

### E9. [V2] $expand
GET {{v2}}/Travellers(guid'{{travellerID}}')?$expand=locations
Authorization: Basic {{traveller1User}} {{traveller1Pass}}


### ==============================================================
### F. $batch — combine multiple reads in one request
### ==============================================================

### F1. [V4] $batch — JSON batch format with two GETs
POST {{v4}}/$batch
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requests": [
    { "id": "1", "method": "GET", "url": "Destinations" },
    { "id": "2", "method": "GET", "url": "TravellerTypes" }
  ]
}

### F2. [V2] $batch — multipart/mixed batch format with one GET
POST {{v2}}/$batch
Authorization: Basic {{adminUser}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: multipart/mixed;boundary=batch_1

--batch_1
Content-Type: application/http
Content-Transfer-Encoding: binary

GET Destinations HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json

--batch_1--
